            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Welcome to CID. You must be the new transfer.",
            "next": "t00-002"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-002",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "First day, right? Don't worry — everyone starts somewhere.",
            "next": "t00-003"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-003",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "I'm Reyes. This is Cho. Between the two of us, you'll be running real cases by the end of the week.",
            "next": "t00-004"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-004",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "This is CID OS — the system every detective in this department uses to run an investigation, start to finish.",
            "next": "t00-005"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-005",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "No paper files, no separate tools scattered across the building. Mail, evidence, maps, cameras — it all lives in one place.",
            "next": "t00-006"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-006",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "I'll show you around CID OS itself. Reyes will walk you through your first real investigation.",
            "next": "t00-007"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-007",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "I've assigned you something small to start — a bookstore break-in. Nothing dangerous. Just enough to learn the ropes.",
            "next": "t00-008"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-008",
            "phase": "welcome",
            "lesson": 1,
            "lessonTitle": "Welcome to CID OS",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Let's start with what's right in front of you. Your desktop.",
            "next": "t00-009"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-009",
            "phase": "desktop",
            "lesson": 2,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding the Desktop",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "This is your desktop. Every icon opens one of our applications — mail, evidence, the board, all of it.",
            "next": "t00-010"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-010",
            "phase": "desktop",
            "lesson": 2,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding the Desktop",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Down there is your taskbar. It shows what's open, and the Start Menu gets you to anything that isn't.",
            "next": "t00-011"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-011",
            "phase": "desktop",
            "lesson": 2,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding the Desktop",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "You can have more than one application open at once, drag windows around, minimize them. It behaves like any workstation should.",
            "next": "t00-012"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-012",
            "phase": "desktop",
            "lesson": 3,
            "lessonTitle": "Opening Applications",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Every case starts in the same place, no matter what it is. Let's open it.",
            "next": "t00-013"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-013",
            "phase": "desktop",
            "lesson": 3,
            "lessonTitle": "Opening Applications",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "instruction",
            "text": "Open Case Management.",
            "requiredAction": {
                "event": "app:opened",
                "match": { "appId": "case-management" }
            },
            "highlightTarget": "[data-app-id=\"case-management\"]",
            "highlightScope": "desktop",
            "next": "t00-014"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-014",
            "phase": "case-management",
            "lesson": 4,
            "lessonTitle": "Case Management",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "This is Case Management. Every case you're assigned, or free to pick up, shows up here.",
            "next": "t00-015"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-015",
            "phase": "case-management",
            "lesson": 4,
            "lessonTitle": "Case Management",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "A case only becomes an Active Investigation once you actually start it. Until then it's just sitting in the list, waiting.",
            "next": "t00-016"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-016",
            "phase": "case-management",
            "lesson": 4,
            "lessonTitle": "Case Management",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Yours is right there — Case 00. Select it.",
            "next": "t00-017"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-017",
            "phase": "case-management",
            "lesson": 4,
            "lessonTitle": "Case Management",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "instruction",
            "text": "Select Case 00.",
            "requiredAction": {
                "event": "case:card-selected",
                "match": { "caseId": "case-00" }
            },
            "highlightTarget": "[data-case-id=\"case-00\"]",
            "highlightScope": "window:case-management",
            "next": "t00-018"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-018",
            "phase": "case-management",
            "lesson": 5,
            "lessonTitle": "Starting an Investigation",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "That's the case brief. Read it whenever you like — but when you're ready, start the investigation. From that point, the system tracks everything for you.",
            "next": "t00-019"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-019",
            "phase": "case-management",
            "lesson": 5,
            "lessonTitle": "Starting an Investigation",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "instruction",
            "text": "Start the investigation.",
            "requiredAction": {
                "event": "investigationStarted",
                "match": { "caseId": "case-00" }
            },
            "highlightTarget": ".casemgmt__detail-action-wrap button, .casemgmt__detail-action-wrap [data-action=\"start\"]",
            "highlightScope": "window:case-management",
            "next": "t00-020"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-020",
            "phase": "active-investigation",
            "lesson": 6,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding Active Investigation",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "There it is. That panel is your Active Investigation. It stays with you no matter which application you open.",
            "next": "t00-021"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-021",
            "phase": "active-investigation",
            "lesson": 6,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding Active Investigation",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "It always shows your current case and your current objective, so you never lose the thread of what to do next.",
            "next": "t00-022"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-022",
            "phase": "active-investigation",
            "lesson": 6,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding Active Investigation",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "You can minimize it if it's in your way. You can't close it while a case is active, though — every application depends on it being there.",
            "next": "t00-023"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-023",
            "phase": "active-investigation",
            "lesson": 6,
            "lessonTitle": "Understanding Active Investigation",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Your first objective is already waiting on that panel. Let's follow it.",
            "next": "t00-024"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-024",
            "phase": "police-mail",
            "lesson": 7,
            "lessonTitle": "Police Mail",
            "speaker": "male-detective",
            "type": "dialogue",
            "text": "Every case starts with a briefing in your inbox. Let's check it.",
            "next": "t00-025"
        },
        {
            "id": "t00-025",
            "phase": "police-mail",
            "lesson": 7,
            "lessonTitle": "Police Mail",
            "speaker": "female-detective",
            "type": "instruction",
            "text": "Open Police Mail.",
            "requiredAction": {
                "event": "app:opened",
                "match": { "appId": "police-mail" }
